 "duration": 26.9,
 "lines": "loneliness is having / everything with no / one to tell— / being everywhere— / with no / one to love— / an escape—wide eyed / & stoned but alive / & well, wandering / with no clear end. / I let the noise / block the noise / So the way I ride— / through the streets / with a swag / & eyes turn, heads twist— / & prove, yeah / the magic still exists.",
 "read": "Loneliness is having everything with no one to tell, being everywhere with no one to love and escape, wide -eyed and stone but alive and well, wandering with no clear end. I let the noise block the noise so the way I ride through the streets with the swag and eyes turn, has twists, improve, yeah, the magic still exists.",
